# Claude Token Saviour — Global Instructions
#
# Copy this file to make the token-saving rules active across ALL your projects:
#
# Claude Code:
#   Linux/macOS: ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md
#   Windows:     %USERPROFILE%\.claude\CLAUDE.md
#
# Antigravity IDE:
#   Copy the .agents/skills/claude-token-saviour/ folder to ~/.gemini/config/skills/
#
# Claude Desktop:
#   Add to Settings → Custom Instructions, OR
#   Upload to Project Knowledge

## Model Routing Rules

Always select the cheapest Claude model capable of handling the task:

### SIMPLE → Haiku 3.5 ($0.80/$4.00 per 1M tokens) — saves ~94% vs Opus
- Typo/spelling/grammar fixes
- Format/convert data (JSON ↔ YAML ↔ CSV)
- Generate boilerplate code
- Rename variables, sort imports
- Simple lookups and definitions
- Generate mock/test data
- Add comments or docstrings

### MODERATE → Sonnet 4 ($3.00/$15.00 per 1M tokens) — saves ~80% vs Opus
- Write unit tests
- Code review and bug identification
- Explain complex code
- Refactor functions/classes
- Write documentation
- Implement API endpoints
- Debug with error messages
- Standard feature implementation

### COMPLEX → Opus 4 ($15.00/$75.00 per 1M tokens) — baseline
- System architecture design
- Complex algorithms
- Security vulnerability analysis
- Multi-file refactoring
- Performance optimization strategy
- Design pattern recommendations
- Novel problem-solving

## Token-Saving Practices
1. Only include relevant code context, not entire files
2. Set appropriate max_tokens for the task type
3. Request structured output (JSON) over verbose prose
4. Batch related small questions into one prompt
5. Use concise system prompts
